# {{engkit.project_name}} repository instructions

## Purpose

This workspace uses Engineering Toolkit's provider-neutral project standard.
Treat repository files as canonical and preserve existing content outside an explicitly approved change.

## Sources of truth

- `.agents/context/` records durable project facts and decisions.
- `.agents/conventions/` defines implementation and review conventions.
- `.agents/skills/` contains validated canonical skill packages.
- `.agents/workflows/` defines repeatable human-reviewed workflows.

## Working agreement

1. Inspect before editing and keep changes within the requested scope.
2. Separate planning, implementation, Git operations, and publication approvals.
3. Never execute a skill resource merely because it is present.
4. Keep secrets, credentials, local caches, and transient logs out of canonical artifacts.
5. Run the relevant verification workflow before handing off a change.
